## DomainErrorException (Web Layer)

Bridge between domain Result failures and HTTP responses:

```java
public class DomainErrorException extends RuntimeException {
    
    private final Error error;
    private final HttpStatus httpStatus;
    
    public DomainErrorException(Error error, HttpStatus httpStatus) {
        super(error.message());
        this.error = error;
        this.httpStatus = httpStatus;
    }
    
    public String getErrorCode() { return error.code(); }
    public HttpStatus getHttpStatus() { return httpStatus; }
}
```

## Controller Error Mapping Pattern

```java
@GetMapping("/search/{backend}")
public ResponseEntity<ContainerSearchResponse> search(
        @PathVariable ExternalApiProvider backend,
        @RequestParam("q") @ValidContainerNumber String containerNumber) {
    
    var query = new SearchContainersQuery(backend, containerNumber, TradeType.IMPORT);
    
    // getOrThrow converts Result.Failure to exception
    var results = dispatcher.dispatch(query)
        .getOrThrow(error -> new DomainErrorException(error, mapErrorToHttpStatus(error)));
    
    return ResponseEntity.ok(ContainerSearchResponse.fromApplication(results));
}

private HttpStatus mapErrorToHttpStatus(Error error) {
    return switch (error.code()) {
        case "Backend.Unsupported", "BulkSearch.EmptyContainerIds" -> HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST;
        case "Container.NotFound" -> HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND;
        case "Search.Failed", "Backend.EModalUnavailable", 
             "Backend.CargoSprintUnavailable", "Backend.ServiceUnavailable" -> HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE;
        default -> HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR;
    };
}
```

## Global Exception Handler

```java
@Slf4j
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

    private static final URI BACKEND_ERROR_TYPE = URI.create("https://cargosprint.com/problems/backend-error");
    private static final URI DOMAIN_ERROR_TYPE = URI.create("https://cargosprint.com/problems/domain-error");
    private static final URI VALIDATION_ERROR_TYPE = URI.create("https://cargosprint.com/problems/validation-error");
    private static final URI CIRCUIT_BREAKER_ERROR_TYPE = URI.create("https://cargosprint.com/problems/circuit-breaker");
    private static final URI RATE_LIMIT_ERROR_TYPE = URI.create("https://cargosprint.com/problems/rate-limit");
    private static final URI SERVER_ERROR_TYPE = URI.create("https://cargosprint.com/problems/server-error");

    @ExceptionHandler(DomainErrorException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleDomainError(DomainErrorException ex) {
        log.warn("Domain error: code={}, message={}", ex.getErrorCode(), ex.getMessage());
        
        var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(ex.getHttpStatus(), ex.getMessage());
        problemDetail.setType(DOMAIN_ERROR_TYPE);
        problemDetail.setTitle(ex.getErrorCode());
        problemDetail.setProperty("errorCode", ex.getErrorCode());
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now().toString());
        
        return ResponseEntity.status(ex.getHttpStatus()).body(problemDetail);
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(BackendServiceException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleBackendServiceException(BackendServiceException ex) {
        log.error("Backend service error: {}", ex.toString(), ex);
        
        var status = ex.getStatusCode() != null
            ? HttpStatus.valueOf(ex.getStatusCode().value())
            : HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE;
        
        var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(status, "Backend service is temporarily unavailable");
        problemDetail.setType(BACKEND_ERROR_TYPE);
        problemDetail.setTitle("Backend Service Error");
        problemDetail.setProperty("service", ex.getServiceName());
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now().toString());
        
        return ResponseEntity.status(status).body(problemDetail);
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleValidationException(MethodArgumentNotValidException ex) {
        log.warn("Validation error: {}", ex.getMessage());
        
        var errors = ex.getBindingResult().getFieldErrors().stream()
            .collect(Collectors.toMap(
                FieldError::getField,
                error -> error.getDefaultMessage() != null ? error.getDefaultMessage() : "Invalid value",
                (existing, replacement) -> existing + "; " + replacement
            ));
        
        var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "Request validation failed");
        problemDetail.setType(VALIDATION_ERROR_TYPE);
        problemDetail.setTitle("Validation Error");
        problemDetail.setProperty("errors", errors);
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now().toString());
        
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST).body(problemDetail);
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(ConstraintViolationException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleConstraintViolation(ConstraintViolationException ex) {
        log.warn("Constraint violation: {}", ex.getMessage());
        
        var errors = ex.getConstraintViolations().stream()
            .collect(Collectors.toMap(
                v -> v.getPropertyPath().toString(),
                ConstraintViolation::getMessage,
                (existing, replacement) -> existing + "; " + replacement
            ));
        
        var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "Request validation failed");
        problemDetail.setType(VALIDATION_ERROR_TYPE);
        problemDetail.setTitle("Validation Error");
        problemDetail.setProperty("errors", errors);
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now().toString());
        
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST).body(problemDetail);
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleTypeMismatch(MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException ex) {
        log.warn("Type mismatch: {}", ex.getMessage());
        
        var requiredType = ex.getRequiredType();
        String errorMessage;
        
        if (requiredType != null && requiredType.isEnum()) {
            var validValues = Arrays.stream(requiredType.getEnumConstants())
                .map(Object::toString)
                .collect(Collectors.joining(", "));
            errorMessage = String.format(
                "Invalid value '%s' for parameter '%s'. Valid values are: %s",
                ex.getValue(), ex.getName(), validValues
            );
        } else {
            errorMessage = String.format(
                "Invalid value '%s' for parameter '%s'",
                ex.getValue(), ex.getName()
            );
        }
        
        var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "Request validation failed");
        problemDetail.setType(VALIDATION_ERROR_TYPE);
        problemDetail.setTitle("Validation Error");
        problemDetail.setProperty("errors", List.of(errorMessage));
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now().toString());
        
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST).body(problemDetail);
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(CallNotPermittedException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleCircuitBreaker(CallNotPermittedException ex) {
        log.error("Circuit breaker open: {}", ex.getMessage());
        
        var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(
            HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE,
            "Service is temporarily unavailable due to high error rate"
        );
        problemDetail.setType(CIRCUIT_BREAKER_ERROR_TYPE);
        problemDetail.setTitle("Service Unavailable");
        problemDetail.setProperty("circuitBreaker", ex.getCausingCircuitBreakerName());
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now().toString());
        
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE).body(problemDetail);
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(RequestNotPermitted.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleRateLimit(RequestNotPermitted ex) {
        log.warn("Rate limit exceeded: {}", ex.getMessage());
        
        var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(
            HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS,
            "Rate limit exceeded, please try again later"
        );
        problemDetail.setType(RATE_LIMIT_ERROR_TYPE);
        problemDetail.setTitle("Rate Limit Exceeded");
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now().toString());
        
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS).body(problemDetail);
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(HttpClientErrorException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleHttpClientError(HttpClientErrorException ex) {
        var statusCode = ex.getStatusCode();
        
        if (statusCode.value() == 401) {
            log.warn("Backend authentication failed (401)");
            var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(
                HttpStatus.UNAUTHORIZED, "Authentication failed - token may be invalid or expired");
            problemDetail.setTitle("Unauthorized");
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.UNAUTHORIZED).body(problemDetail);
        }
        
        if (statusCode.value() == 403) {
            log.warn("Backend authorization failed (403)");
            var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(
                HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN, "Access denied - insufficient permissions");
            problemDetail.setTitle("Forbidden");
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN).body(problemDetail);
        }
        
        log.warn("HTTP client error: {}", statusCode);
        var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(
            HttpStatus.valueOf(statusCode.value()), "Backend request failed");
        problemDetail.setType(BACKEND_ERROR_TYPE);
        return ResponseEntity.status(statusCode).body(problemDetail);
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleGenericException(Exception ex) {
        // Log full exception at ERROR level, don't expose details to client
        log.error("Unhandled exception occurred", ex);
        
        var problemDetail = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(
            HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,
            "An unexpected error occurred"
        );
        problemDetail.setType(SERVER_ERROR_TYPE);
        problemDetail.setTitle("Internal Server Error");
        problemDetail.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now().toString());
        
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR).body(problemDetail);
    }
}
```

## ProblemDetail Response Format (RFC 7807)

```json
{
    "type": "https://cargosprint.com/problems/domain-error",
    "title": "Container.NotFound",
    "status": 404,
    "detail": "Container not found",
    "instance": "/api/bff/containers/search/EMODAL",
    "errorCode": "Container.NotFound",
    "timestamp": "2025-01-08T10:30:00Z"
}
```

## Conventions

- NEVER expose stack traces or internal details in production
- Use `ProblemDetail` (RFC 7807) for ALL error responses
- Log exceptions with correlation IDs (see `logging.mdc`)
- Handle specific exceptions first, generic `Exception` last
- Domain errors use Result pattern â€” NOT exceptions
- Use `DomainErrorException` to bridge Result failures to HTTP
- Use `@RestControllerAdvice` for global exception handling
- Include timestamp in all error responses
- Include error code for programmatic handling

**See also:** `logging.mdc`, `cqrs.mdc`, `resilience.mdc`
